-- title:
--   Branch reading gives an embedding of the full level-M' field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`), and let $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   The following data are fixed.
--
--   *Reduction frame.* A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,M' = \kappa_A(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_{M'})$ over $\kappa_A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'`$\kappa_A$ (`hW`), an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$) into `fieldBar q M'` (the base change of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`), a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with respect to $A$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC`$\kappa_A\,M'$ — that is, a valuation subring $R_0$.`integers` of the big field, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0$.`residue` onto the residue target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders of functions, together with the compatibilities with $A$ and its residue field recorded in the structure — the hypothesis `hR₀` stating that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral with residue obtained by reducing coefficients through $A \to \kappa_A$, and an element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   *Small constants.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); furthermore `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Cyclotomic data and the level field.* An element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), together with `hιξ`, the existence of a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$; a subgroup $H_1$ of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ equal to the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$ (`hH₁`); an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((\mathfrak q))/k_0$ equal to the $k_0$-base change of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ (`hK`), an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $k_0$, and $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficient image of the $q$-expansion `jq` (`hj`), assumed non-zero.
--
--   *Functoriality hypotheses for the rigid datum.* Three universally quantified hypotheses over commutative $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` (the conditions that $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the Weierstrass equation, that `W.preΨ ℓg` vanishes at $x_P$, and that $(x_Q,y_Q) = (x_P,y_P)$) is preserved under a variable change $C$ acting simultaneously on $W$ and on the level datum; `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is preserved on replacing $h$ by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and `hL`, that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` by $h$ is preserved by the same transformation of $h$, with $x$ replaced by $u^{-2}(x-r)$.
--
--   *Drinfeld data.* Group laws $\mathcal G$ on $A_0$ with `IsChordTangent` (`h𝒢`) and `IsOriginIdentity` (`h𝒢O`), and a `LevelTransport` $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ with `IsSectionTransport` (`h𝒯`); the hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra and every projective Weierstrass curve, graded ring homomorphisms on the projective model rings realising variable changes (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and coefficient maps along $A_0$-algebra maps (`IsCoefficientHom`), each carrying the irrelevant ideal into the image of the irrelevant ideal.
--
--   *Moduli package and the pinned Tate point.* Write $R =$ `rigidDataH1Pow`$A_0\ \ell_g\ M'\ q$ (built from `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL`, $\mathcal G$, $\mathcal T$), the rigid Weierstrass datum whose level structure combines a $\Gamma_0$-power component for $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point and a Drinfeld level-$q$ pair, restricted by the link condition. Fixed are an absolute fine moduli package $P_0$ for the associated `LevelModuliDatum` (a commutative $A_0$-algebra $P_0.B_0$ with a universal point representing all points functorially), a point $x_0$ of that datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant `jOf` $x_0$ equals `jqNModC`$k_0\ q$ as a Laurent series (`hx₀`), an $A_0$-algebra map `clC` from $P_0.B_0$ to the chart algebra `chartAlgFin`$A_0\ K\ j$ (the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ generated in the two-chart integral model by $j$) whose composition with the inclusion into $K$ is the classifying map $P_0$.`classify` $x_0$ (`hclC`), and the pinning hypothesis `hμ`: there exist a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ and a raw point $r$ of $R$ over $K$ with $\mathrm{Quot.mk}\,r = x_0$, such that (i) the normalisation conditions hold, namely the explicit relation between $u$, the coordinates of the toric point `tateToricPoint`$k_0\ q$ at $\xi^q$ and the constants $1/6$, together with $r = -1/12$, $s = -1/2$, $t = 1/24$; (ii) the Weierstrass curve of $r$ becomes $C \cdot$ `tateBase`$k_0\ q$ over $k_0((\mathfrak q))$; (iii) for every prime $p \mid M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-power component of $r$ maps to the variable-change transform of the explicit product $\prod_a (X - x(\zeta^a))$ over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$, the $x$-coordinates being those of `toricPoint`$F'\ q$; (iv) the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $r$ becomes the variable-change transform of the `LevelPData` all of whose entries are the coordinates of the toric point at $\xi^q$; and (v) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ equal to the four entries of the variable-change transform of `cuspData`$k_0\ q\ \xi^{\ell_g}$ at the vectors $(1,0)$ and $(0,-1)$ over $\mathbb Z/q$, with the Drinfeld sections $P$ and $Q$ of $r$ passing through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   *Residue embedding.* A ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the residue field of $A_0$ to $\kappa_A$ compatible with the two residue maps (`hθ`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of the chart algebra $C :=$ `chartAlgFin`$A_0\ K\ j$, let $\psi : C \to$ `ResidueField`$A_0$ be an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism whose zero set is exactly $y$, let $\Omega$ be a field extension of $\kappa_A$, let $V$ be a place of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$, let $\mathrm{res}$ be a ring homomorphism from the residue field of the valuation ring of $V$ to $\kappa_A$ and $\rho : C \to \mathcal O_V$ a ring homomorphism, subject to: `hr`, that $\mathrm{res}$ retracts the structure map $\kappa_A \to$ `ResidueField`$\mathcal O_V$; `hs`, that on $A_0$ the composite $\rho$ followed by the inclusion $\mathcal O_V \to \Omega$ agrees with $\theta$ composed with the reduction of $A_0$ and the structure map $\kappa_A \to \Omega$; `hp`, that $\mathrm{res} \circ \mathrm{residue}_V \circ \rho = \theta \circ \psi$ on $C$; and `ht`, that the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho($`jChartFin`$A_0\ K\ j)$ is transcendental over $\kappa_A$.
--
--   Then there exists a $\kappa_A$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{emb}$ from `modularFunctionFieldFullC`$\kappa_A\ M'$ (the field generated over $\kappa_A$ by the divisor expansions of level $M'$) to $\Omega$ with the following two properties.
--
--   First, for every Laurent series $gf$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficient image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0$.`integers`, and which is cusp-regular in the sense that every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image of `jq` non-negative also has $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image of $gf$ non-negative: whenever the coefficient image of $gf$ in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ lies in $K$ and the resulting element of $K$ lies in the chart algebra $C$, the value of $\mathrm{emb}$ at the image of $R_0$.`residue` of $gf$ under the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldC`$\kappa_A\ M' \le$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC`$\kappa_A\ M'$ equals the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho$ applied to that element of $C$.
--
--   Second, for every positive $d$ dividing $M'$, whenever the coefficient image of `qExpand`$\mathbb Q\ d\$`jq` lies in $K$ and the resulting element lies in $C$, then $\mathrm{emb}($`jqNFull`$\kappa_A\ M'\ d)$ equals the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho$ applied to that element.
--
--   This is the step in the full-level Diamond frame which converts a branch of the integral two-chart model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$, read through a place $V$ of $\Omega$ at which the $j$-coordinate stays transcendental, into an embedding into $\Omega$ of the whole level-$M'$ modular function field in characteristic $q$, normalised so that the reductions of admissible (integral, cusp-regular) rational modular functions and the functions $\tilde\jmath(\mathfrak q^d)$, $d \mid M'$, are read off by $\rho$. It is used in the construction of moduli places compatible with Frobenius for the pinned Tate point of the rigid $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-datum.
